SUMMARY:Deadline: Oregon Media Arts Fellowship 2026 (two USD 5\,000 awards 
 for Oregon media artists)
DESCRIPTION:The Oregon Media Arts Fellowship\, run by the Portland Art Muse
 um's Center for an Untold Tomorrow with the Oregon Arts Commission\, gives
  Oregon media artists money to create or complete new work.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Portland Art Museum (PAM CUT) and Oregon Arts Commission\nLocation: Ore
 gon\, United States (Oregon residents only).\nAward: Two fellowships of US
 D 5\,000 each\, no matching funds required\; paid within two months of not
 ification. No application fee.\nDuration: One-time award for new work or w
 orks in progress.\n\nMore: https://portlandartmuseum.org/artist-services/o
 regon-media-arts-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/artist-services/oregon-media-arts-fellows
 hip/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oregon\, United States (Oregon residents only).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:att-untold-stories-tribeca-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261116T154227Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: AT&T Untold Stories 2027 (Tribeca Festival): USD 1.2 mill
 ion film production prize
DESCRIPTION:AT&T Untold Stories\, now in its 10th year\, is a production pr
 ize run by the Tribeca Festival and AT&T that funds a feature film from an
  underrepresented filmmaker. Industry judges select five projects\; their 
 filmmakers pitch to a jury of media professionals at the 2027 Tribeca Fest
 ival in June. One project wins USD 1.2 million and the other four finalist
 s receive USD 15\,000 each.\n\nOrganisation: Tribeca Festival and AT&T\nLo
 cation: USA. Applicants must be 18+ and live in the US or Puerto Rico. Fin
 alists pitch in person at the Tribeca Festival\, New York\, June 2027.\nAw
 ard: One winner receives USD 1\,200\,000 to produce the film\; the four ot
 her finalists receive USD 15\,000 grants each. No entry fee.\n\nMore: http
 s://tribecafilm.com/attuntoldstories?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tribecafilm.com/attuntoldstories?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA. Applicants must be 18+ and live in the US or Puerto Rico. Fin
 alists pitch in person at the Tribeca Festival\, New York\, June 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tag-queer-shorts-festival-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261116T154227Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tag! Queer Shorts Festival 2027: Call for Submissions (Po
 rtland)
DESCRIPTION:Tag! invites LGBTQIA+ filmmakers to submit finished shorts of 1
 5 minutes or under\, including credits\, in any genre (theme for 2027: "Yo
 u're It!"). About 40 to 45 shorts are selected. English captions are requi
 red\; films made with generative AI are not programmed\; no works in progr
 ess. Submissions open 1 July to 1 December 2026\, exclusively via FilmFree
 way.\n\nOrganisation: Tag! Queer Shorts Festival\nLocation: Portland\, Ore
 gon\, USA (Clinton Street Theater). International.\nAward: Award categorie
 s with cash prizes (amounts not stated): Hispanic/Latine Creativity\, Powe
 r of Community\, Best Erotic Short and Radical Futures Student Film\, plus
  a Festival Director's Award. Modest submission fees on FilmFreeway\; fee 
 waivers for historically excluded communities and filmmakers from countrie
 s that criminalize queer identities\, and discount codes for Pacific North
 west filmmakers.\nDuration: Festival 20 and 21 March 2027\n\nMore: https:/
 /tagqsf.org/call-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://tagqsf.org/call-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Portland\, Oregon\, USA (Clinton Street Theater). International.
END:VEVENT
